          "secNumber": "2.3",
          "heading": "Stacks",
          "content": "### Stacks\n\nA last-in-first-out stack supports push, pop, and peek. It is used in expression parsing, depth-first search, and call management. Its contract must specify whether popping an empty stack raises an exception or returns a distinguished result.",
          "simulations": []
